{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794428077,"nonce":"7aIPvOKOgtmNmPdPLAU4AZa82Z8=","title":"x","message":"Follow-up to df660b6 item 3, filed 2026-11-12 by the review of fix/build-fork-and-context.\n\nQuestion: with BuildKit's `--oci-worker-no-process-sandbox` (crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs, BUILDKITD_FLAGS), can a Dockerfile `RUN` step read the registry credential mounted at /scarab/registry in the build container?\n\nMeasured 2026-11-12 on a colima VM (Ubuntu kernel 6.8.0-117, Yama `kernel.yama.ptrace_scope=1`), moby/buildkit:rootless digest sha256:5987568f…, run as uid 1000 with seccomp and AppArmor unconfined, as the executor does:\n- A RUN step sees the outer PID namespace: pid 1 is buildctl-daemonless.sh, and rootlesskit, buildkitd, buildkit-runc and the buildctl client are all listed, with readable cmdlines.\n- `/proc/\u003cpid\u003e/root/scarab/registry/config.json` and `/proc/\u003cpid\u003e/environ` are refused for every one of them (RUN runs as root in BuildKit's user namespace, which maps to the same outer uid 1000).\n- So: no leak with Yama scope 1.\n\nNot measured: Yama scope 0. Under scope 1, a process may read another's /proc root only if it is an ancestor; the RUN step is a descendant of buildkitd, so that rule alone may be what blocks it. EKS AL2023 is Fedora-based and may default to 0. Changing the VM's sysctl to test was refused by the session's safety settings; it needs the owner (or a throwaway VM / the kind node).\n\nTo do:\n1. Check `kernel.yama.ptrace_scope` on an AL2023 EKS node and on the kind node.\n2. Repeat the probe with scope 0 (throwaway VM). The probe is a Dockerfile whose RUN loops over /proc/[0-9]* and cats `$p/root/scarab/registry/config.json` and greps `$p/environ`.\n3. If it leaks: move the credential out of the build container (e.g. a second container does the push, or buildctl gets auth through a socket only it can reach), or run BuildKit with its process sandbox where the cluster allows it.\n4. Prove the guard (BUILD_GUARD) in the real image: the unit test runs the host's sh, not busybox. A kind-tier test (`just test e2e` build case) with a committed symlink context should be refused.","files":null}]}